{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And the fire upon the altar shall burn on it.</b> Scripture multiplied many burnings here — <b>upon its burning, and the fire of the altar shall burn on it, and the fire upon the altar shall burn on it, a fire shall continually burn upon the altar</b> — all of them are expounded in tractate Yoma (45a), where our Rabbis disagreed concerning the number of ma'arachot that were there." "<b>And arrange upon it the burnt offering.</b> It is the daily burnt offering that precedes (Menachot 49a)." "<b>The fats of the shelamim.</b> If they bring shelamim there — and our Rabbis learned from here, ״upon it״ — upon the morning burnt offering, all the offerings are completed; from here that nothing may come after the tamid of between the evenings (Sifra)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:05:11.966412521Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}